          "role": "assistant",
          "reasoning_content": "We need answer solve. Need step-by-step. Let's solve.\n\nEquation1: 2^{x+1}=4^{x-7}=(2^2)^{x-7}=2^{2x-14}. Equate exponents: x+1=2x-14 => x=15.\n\nEquation2: 8^{3y}=16^{-y+13}. Bases powers 2: 8=2^3, 16=2^4. LHS=2^{9y}. RHS=2^{4(-y+13)}=2^{-4y+52}. Equate: 9y=-4y+52 =>13y=52=>y=4.\n\nx+y=19. Need step by step end exact phrase.",
          "content": "\\[\n2^{x+1}=4^{x-7}\n\\]\nSince \\(4=2^2\\),\n\\[\n4^{x-7}=(2^2)^{x-7}=2^{2x-14}\n\\]\nSo,\n\\[\n2^{x+1}=2^{2x-14}\n\\]\nEquate exponents:\n\\[\nx+1=2x-14\n\\]\n\\[\nx=15\n\\]\n\nNow,\n\\[\n8^{3y}=16^{-y+13}\n\\]\nSince \\(8=2^3\\) and \\(16=2^4\\),\n\\[\n8^{3y}=(2^3)^{3y}=2^{9y}\n\\]\n\\[\n16^{-y+13}=(2^4)^{-y+13}=2^{-4y+52}\n\\]\nSo,\n\\[\n2^{9y}=2^{-4y+52}\n\\]\nEquate exponents:\n\\[\n9y=-4y+52\n\\]\n\\[\n13y=52\n\\]\n\\[\ny=4\n\\]\n\nTherefore,\n\\[\nx+y=15+4=19\n\\]\n\nThe answer is 19."
